                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I gave a negative review for Archangel some days ago, despite being an highly spectacular VR game (with a serious budget behind) the gameplay was basic and flat, with small enemies, no robot-vs-robot fighting and almost zero freedom. Very curious than War Robots VR: The Skirmish, being a free demo and with an evident lower budget, without motion controller support, is instead an a wonderful mech game than is just on the target.\n\nControls are ultra simplified, but works flawlessy. Head aiming is used also for turning, and actually this solution works better than I expected. Joystick is used for walk and strafing, and triggers for submachine and rocket launcher. The game is set in a town, and there are multiple robots in it, friendly and not. There is also a bit of story, even if the demo is just a couple of minutes long. The graphic is good, you get a proper sense of scale (those robots are just a few meters, not building size like in Archangel) and mechs are properly animated. \n\nFor those who played Vox Machinae with Oculus DK2, this is very much the same but MUCH better. For those disappointed from Archangel, this is the game to play. What actually worries me is than this pearl is free, and I want to know more about a full game of this kind (the demo ends promoting the mobile version of War Robots).",
